17592186045417] [17592186561060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561060 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561060 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1a/1a91d10c69c8d466b6155f775ebd0856003889089cc41a3246ec0a812b58def3.png)\n\nThe graph of the polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The degree of $P(x)$ is odd.\n\nII. $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIII. The coefficient of the leading term is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f2a8f457-b09c-537d-9f0d-5fb2f3f9943c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561060 #edb/ref 1074 "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
